sequenceDiagram
    actor Client
    participant DispatcherServlet
    participant HeaderTenantInterceptor
    participant ThreadTenantStorage
    participant Controller
    participant Repository
    participant Database

    Note over Client,Database: Request Processing with Tenant Context

    Client->>DispatcherServlet: HTTP Request with XTenantID header
    Note right of DispatcherServlet: Request arrives at Spring DispatcherServlet XTenantID: tenant123

    DispatcherServlet->>HeaderTenantInterceptor: preHandle(request, response, handler)
    Note right of HeaderTenantInterceptor: Interceptor intercepts request before handler execution

    HeaderTenantInterceptor->>HeaderTenantInterceptor: Extract tenant header from request
    Note right of HeaderTenantInterceptor: Step 1: Extract XTenantID header value headerName: XTenantID

    HeaderTenantInterceptor->>ThreadTenantStorage: setTenantId(tenantId)
    Note right of ThreadTenantStorage: Step 2: Store tenant ID in ThreadLocal storage tenantId: tenant123

    ThreadTenantStorage->>ThreadTenantStorage: ThreadLocal.set(tenantId)
    Note right of ThreadTenantStorage: Store tenant identifier in ThreadLocal variable tenantId: tenant123

    alt Missing XTenantID header
        HeaderTenantInterceptor->>HeaderTenantInterceptor: Handle missing tenant header
        Note right of HeaderTenantInterceptor: Tenant header not found in request
        HeaderTenantInterceptor-->>Client: HTTP 400 Bad Request
        Note right of Client: Request rejected due to missing tenant context
    else XTenantID header present
        DispatcherServlet->>Controller: Handle request with tenant context
        Note right of Controller: Step 3: Request processing continues with tenant context established

        Controller->>ThreadTenantStorage: getTenantId()
        ThreadTenantStorage-->>Controller: tenant123
        Note right of Controller: Controller retrieves tenant context for business logic

        alt Exception during request processing
            Controller->>Controller: Throw exception
            Note right of Controller: Exception thrown during business logic
            DispatcherServlet->>HeaderTenantInterceptor: afterCompletion(request, response, handler, exception)
            Note right of HeaderTenantInterceptor: Interceptor still called for cleanup
            HeaderTenantInterceptor->>ThreadTenantStorage: clear()
            Note right of ThreadTenantStorage: Cleanup still executed to prevent ThreadLocal leak
        else Normal flow
            Controller->>Repository: findById(id) or save(entity)
            Note right of Repository: Repository operations execute with tenant context tenantContext: tenant123

            Repository->>Database: Execute SQL with tenant filter
            Note right of Database: Database query includes tenant isolation sql: SELECT * FROM authors WHERE tenantid = tenant123

            Database-->>Repository: Return query results
            Note right of Repository: Database returns filtered results

            Repository-->>Controller: Return entity or collection
            Note right of Controller: Repository returns processed results

            Controller-->>DispatcherServlet: Return response
            Note right of DispatcherServlet: Controller returns response to DispatcherServlet

            DispatcherServlet->>HeaderTenantInterceptor: postHandle(request, response, handler, modelAndView)
            Note right of HeaderTenantInterceptor: Step 3: Postprocessing after handler execution

            DispatcherServlet->>HeaderTenantInterceptor: afterCompletion(request, response, handler, exception)
            Note right of HeaderTenantInterceptor: Step 4: Cleanup after request completion

            HeaderTenantInterceptor->>ThreadTenantStorage: clear()
            Note right of ThreadTenantStorage: Step 4: Clear ThreadLocal storage

            ThreadTenantStorage->>ThreadTenantStorage: ThreadLocal.remove()
            Note right of ThreadTenantStorage: Remove tenant identifier from ThreadLocal

            DispatcherServlet-->>Client: HTTP Response
            Note right of Client: Step 5: Request processing complete, response sent to client
        end
    end